      "title": "Token Service: Troubleshooting Unexpected 401/403 Errors and Access Issues",
      "content_summary": "Provides broad troubleshooting guidance for HTTP 401/403 errors, incorrect data visibility, or unexpected privilege escalations within the Token Service, focusing on configuration and policy checks.",
      "content_body": "When users encounter 'permission denied' messages or see unexpected HTTP 401/403 errors, first verify the user's role assignments and ensure no conditional access policies are blocking the request. Check the application scope and consent details to confirm they match the intended resource permissions. Often, these issues stem from improper access reviews or operator errors during configuration changes. Resolving these incidents typically requires a policy correction, updating permissions, or completing a scheduled access review. Educate customers on the correct flow for requesting access if the issue results from misunderstanding the authorization model."
